\name{identify_levels_ExtFunType}
\alias{identify_levels_ExtFunType}
\title{Identify Bouts for External Function Type Classifications}
\description{
Identifies bouts for epoch-by-epoch categorical classifications generated by
external functions with \code{reporttype = "type"} in GGIR Part 5.

The function converts the external function type information stored in the
Part 5 time series into a representation suitable for subsequent summary
analysis. It creates epoch-level type durations and identifies bouts for
each classification type according to the specified bout duration,
bout criterion, and type priority.
}
\usage{
identify_levels_ExtFunType(ts, myfun, ws3)
}
\arguments{
\item{ts}{
Data frame containing the Part 5 epoch-level time series, including the
columns generated for external function type classifications.
}
\item{myfun}{
List defining the external function. The function uses
\code{reporttype}, \code{colnames}, \code{tbout.dur},
\code{tbout.criter}, and \code{tbout.order} when available.
}
\item{ws3}{
Numeric value specifying the epoch duration in seconds.
}
}
\value{
A list containing:
\describe{
\item{\code{TLEVELS}}{
A list containing the bout masks for each external function type.
Each element is a matrix with one row for each bout-duration definition
and one column for each epoch. Values of 1 indicate epochs included in
the corresponding bout.
}
\item{\code{TOLEVELS}}{
A matrix containing the number of seconds in each epoch assigned to each
external function type. Columns represent classification types and rows
represent epochs.
}
\item{\code{Tnames}}{
A character vector containing the names corresponding to the bout
definitions stored in \code{TLEVELS}.
}
}
\details{
The function is used internally by \code{identify_levels} when an external
function has \code{reporttype = "type"}.

Type classifications are represented using the \code{ExtFunType_*_s}
columns in \code{ts}. Classification names are treated case-insensitively.

If \code{tbout.dur} is not specified, the default bout durations are
\code{c(1, 5, 10)} minutes. If \code{tbout.criter} is not specified, the
default bout criterion is 0.8. If \code{tbout.order} is not specified, the
classification types are ordered alphabetically.

Bout durations are processed from longest to shortest. When multiple
classification types overlap, the order specified by \code{tbout.order}
determines the priority with which epochs are assigned to bouts.

The function does not split bouts according to sleep period time or daytime.
The resulting bout masks can therefore span these boundaries and are
subsequently restricted to the relevant period during Part 5 analysis.

The function is intended to be called internally and is not normally called
directly by users.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{identify_levels}},
\code{\link{g.part5_analyseSegment_ExtFunType}}
}
